                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="816-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>beyerdynamic Opus 88</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Opus 88 is a miniature electret condenser mic with an integrated spring-loaded clamp, intended for mounting on drum rims. The electret capsule is mounted atop a 75mm gooseneck, facilitating positioning above the drum.</p><p>It is a variant of the Opus 87 and shares all the 87&#8217;s performance specifications. The only differences are physical:</p><ul><li>The Opus 88 has a 20mm gooseneck, whereas the Opus 87 has a 75mm gooseneck.</li><li>The Opus 88 gooseneck has a swivel mount, allowing the gooseneck to be rotated clock-hand style across the drum head. The Opus 87 does not have this feature, as its gooseneck protrudes directly from the clip mount rather than being attached at 90&deg;.</li><li>The rim clamps are different sizes; the Opus 88 clamp measures 85mm x 118mm, while the Opus 87 clamp measures 85mm x 102mm.</li></ul><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/beyerdynamic/Opus-88">beyerdynamic Opus-88</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2005.</p>
